T Six-axis K'NEX robot arm, all axes driven by mechanical linear actuators
# U = 37.5 mm, z up, desk at z = 0. Every axis is the same mechanism: a rod that slides through two
# guide hubs (the linear actuator), a yoke at its end carrying a pin, a coupler link with a hub at
# each end, and a crank pin on the link being driven. Two opposed rubber bands centre each slider so
# the arm holds a pose with no input; the F lines are the push/pull input and are declared at 0.01 N
# so that pressing one with a gain of 300 is a 3 N push and the settle stays neutral.
! base deck: a 4U square with a rear extension for ballast. The outer nodes are 3D pairs, because a
! horizontal deck rod and a vertical leg are never coplanar.
C P1 B7 2,2,1.5 z -x
C P1v B7 2,2,1.5 x -z
C P2 B7 2,-2,1.5 z y
C P2v B7 2,-2,1.5 x -z
C P3 W8 -2,-2,1.5
C P4 W8 -2,2,1.5
C P5 W8 -2,0,1.5
C GB3 W8 -3,-2,1.5
C R1 B7 -4,-2,1.5 z x
C R1v B7 -4,-2,1.5 x -z
C R2 B7 -4,2,1.5 z -y
C R2v B7 -4,2,1.5 x -z
C R3 W8 -4,0,1.5
R P1 P2
R P2 P3
R P4 P1
R P3 P5
R P5 P4
R P3 GB3
R GB3 R1
R P5 R3
R P4 R2
R R1 R3
R R3 R2
R R1 P5
R P5 R2
! the centre node is a 3D pair too: the deck rods lie in its plane, the yaw axle stands on its partner
C BC B7 0,0,1.5 z x+y
C BCV B7 0,0,1.5 y z
R BC P1
R BC P2
R BC P3
R BC P4
R BC P5
! feet: the only parts that touch the desk
C FT1 W8 2,2,0.5 x y
C FT2 W8 2,-2,0.5 x y
C FT5 W8 -4,-2,0.5 x y
C FT6 W8 -4,2,0.5 x y
R FT1 P1v
R FT2 P2v
R FT5 R1v
R FT6 R2v
! ballast at the back, so the reach of the arm does not tip it
W ballastL R1 mass=400
W ballastR R2 mass=400
! AXIS 1 bearing: a red rod standing on the centre pair, capped at the top
R BCV 0,0,5.5 red
C YCAP D1 0,0,5.5 y -z
! the column: a braced box riding two hubs on that axle. The spacers under the lower hub turn the
! bearing into a thrust bearing so the column cannot slide down the axle.
H Y1 W8 0,0,2.5
H Y2 W8 0,0,4.5
P 0,0,2.3 silver
P 0,0,2.7 silver
C CA B7 1,1,2.5 z -x
C CAv B7 1,1,2.5 x z
C CB B7 1,-1,2.5 z y
C CBv B7 1,-1,2.5 -y z
C CC B7 -1,-1,2.5 z x
C CCv B7 -1,-1,2.5 -x z
C CD B7 -1,1,2.5 z -y
C CDv B7 -1,1,2.5 y z
R Y1 CA
R Y1 CB
R Y1 CC
R Y1 CD
R CA CB
R CB CC
R CC CD
R CD CA
C CA2 B7 1,1,4.5 z -x
C CA2v B7 1,1,4.5 y -z
C CB2 B7 1,-1,4.5 z y
C CB2v B7 1,-1,4.5 x -z
C CC2 B7 -1,-1,4.5 z x-y
C CC2v B7 -1,-1,4.5 -y -z
C CD2 B7 -1,1,4.5 z -y
C CD2v B7 -1,1,4.5 -x -z
R Y2 CA2
R Y2 CB2
R Y2 CC2
R Y2 CD2
R CA2 CB2
R CB2 CC2
R CC2 CD2
R CD2 CA2
! four uprights and four face diagonals, one starting and one landing at every corner
R CAv CA2v
R CBv CB2v
R CCv CC2v
R CDv CD2v
R CAv CB2v
R CBv CC2v
R CCv CD2v
R CDv CA2v
! AXIS 1 crank: a triangulated arm off the column top reaching 2U behind the axle, with a pin
! hanging from its tip. The coupler runs parallel to the slide, which is where the torque comes from.
C CK2 B7 0,-2,4.5 z x
C CK2v B7 0,-2,4.5 x -z
R CB2 CK2
R CC2 CK2
C CKC D1 0,-2,3.5 x z
R CK2v CKC
H CY2 W8 0,-2,4
P 0,-2,3.8 silver
P 0,-2,4.2 silver
! AXIS 1 actuator: a red rod sliding along x at y=-2, z=2.5, with its yoke pin standing up to z=4.5
H CY1 W8 -2,-2,4
P -2,-2,3.8 silver
P -2,-2,4.2 silver
R CY1 CY2
C YK1 R3 -2,-2,2.5 y -x
C PC1 D1 -2,-2,4.5 x -z
R YK1 PC1
C AC1 D1 -6,-2,2.5 y x
R YK1 AC1
H GH1 W8 -3,-2,2.5
H GH2 W8 -4,-2,2.5
R GH1 GB3
R GH2 R1v
! opposed centring bands
E yawA1 AC1 R1 rest=68 k=0.08
E yawA2 AC1 R1 rest=68 k=0.08
E yawB1 YK1 GB3 rest=30 k=0.08
E yawB2 YK1 GB3 rest=30 k=0.08
F AC1 0.01,0,0 yaw
F GH1 -0.01,0,0 yawr
! AXIS 2 shoulder: a hub on the front rail of the column top. The upper arm is a flat triangle in the
! plane y=0; the crank is the arm itself, with the pin 2U out from the bearing.
H SH W8 1,0,4.5
P 1,-0.2,4.5 silver
P 1,0.2,4.5 silver
C MIDU W8 2,0,4.5
C UA B7 3,0,4.5 y -x
C UAv B7 3,0,4.5 z -y
C EL B7 3,0,6.5 y -z
C ELv B7 3,0,6.5 z y
R SH MIDU
R MIDU UA
R UA EL
R SH EL
! crank pin on the upper arm, coupler down and back to the slider
C SCC D1 3,-2,4.5 x y
R UAv SCC
H SCP W8 3,-1,4.5
P 3,-0.8,4.5 silver
P 3,-1.2,4.5 silver
H SAP W8 1,-1,6.5
P 1,-0.8,6.5 silver
P 1,-1.2,6.5 silver
R SCP SAP
! AXIS 2 actuator: a red rod sliding vertically at x=1, y=-2, guided by a hub braced into the
! horizontal triangle of the column top
C YK2 R3 1,-2,6.5 x -z
C PC2 D1 1,0,6.5 x -y
R YK2 PC2
C AS1 D1 1,-2,2.5 x z
R YK2 AS1
H GS1 W8 1,-2,4.5
R GS1 CB2
R GS1 CK2
E shoA YK2 CB2 rest=82 k=0.12
E shoB1 AS1 CB2 rest=35 k=0.055
E shoB2 AS1 CB2 rest=35 k=0.055
E shoB3 AS1 CB2 rest=35 k=0.055
F AS1 0,0,0.01 shoulder
F GS1 0,0,-0.01 shoulderr
! AXIS 3 elbow: axle cantilevered off the elbow node, forearm as an A-frame in the plane y=1
C ECAP D1 3,2,6.5 x -y
R ELv ECAP
H FH W8 3,1,6.5
P 3,0.8,6.5 silver
P 3,1.2,6.5 silver
C FK B7 5,1,6.5 y -x-z
C FKv B7 5,1,6.5 z y
C FB W8 4,1,5.5
R FH FK
R FH FB
R FB FK
! crank pin at the far end of the forearm, coupler back and down to the slider
C ECC D1 5,3,6.5 x -y
R FKv ECC
H ECP W8 5,2,6.5
P 5,1.8,6.5 silver
P 5,2.2,6.5 silver
H EAP W8 3,2,4.5
P 3,1.8,4.5 silver
P 3,2.2,4.5 silver
R ECP EAP
! AXIS 3 actuator: a red rod sliding along x at y=3, z=4.5, guided off a bracket on the upper arm
C YK3 R3 3,3,4.5 z -x
C PC3 D1 3,1,4.5 x y
R YK3 PC3
C AE1 D1 -1,3,4.5 y x
R YK3 AE1
H GE1 W8 2,3,4.5
C BRB W8 2,1,4.5
R GE1 BRB
R BRB MIDU
R BRB UAv
E elbA YK3 GE1 rest=28
E elbB AE1 GE1 rest=76
F AE1 0.01,0,0 elbow
F GE1 -0.01,0,0 elbowr
! mast on the forearm, carrying the two guides of the wrist-pitch actuator
C MB W8 1,1,6.5
C MA B7 2,1,7.5 y x-z
C MAv B7 2,1,7.5 z y
C MD B7 1,1,7.5 y -z
C MDv B7 1,1,7.5 z y
R FH MB
R FH MA
R MB MA
R MB MD
R MA MD
! AXIS 4 wrist pitch: axle cantilevered off the forearm elbow node, wrist link is a triangle at y=0
C WCAP D1 5,-1,6.5 x y
R FKv WCAP
H WH W8 5,0,6.5
P 5,-0.2,6.5 silver
P 5,0.2,6.5 silver
C WT B7 6,0,7.5 y -x-z
C WTv B7 6,0,7.5 z y
C WA W8 7,0,6.5
R WH WT
R WT WA
R WH WA
C W4CC D1 6,2,7.5 x -y
R WTv W4CC
H W4C W8 6,1,7.5
P 6,0.8,7.5 silver
P 6,1.2,7.5 silver
H W4A W8 4,1,7.5
P 4,0.8,7.5 silver
P 4,1.2,7.5 silver
R W4A W4C
C YK4 R3 4,2,7.5 z -x
C PC4 D1 4,0,7.5 x y
R YK4 PC4
C AE4 D1 0,2,7.5 y x
R YK4 AE4
H GW1 W8 2,2,7.5
H GW2 W8 1,2,7.5
R GW1 MAv
R GW2 MDv
E wriA1 YK4 GW1 rest=15 k=0.035
E wriA2 YK4 GW1 rest=15 k=0.035
E wriB AE4 GW1 rest=73 k=0.07
F AE4 0.01,0,0 wrist
F GW1 -0.01,0,0 wristr
! AXIS 5 wrist roll: the hand rides a hub on a shaft along the arm's own axis
C RCAP R3 9,0,6.5 y -z
R WA RCAP
H RH W8 8,0,6.5
P 7.8,0,6.5 silver
P 8.2,0,6.5 silver
C HU W8 8,0,7.5 x -z
C HL B7 8,0,5.5 x y+z
C HLv B7 8,0,5.5 z -x
C HR W8 8,1,6.5
C HB B7 8,-1,6.5 x y-z
C HBv B7 8,-1,6.5 z x
R RH HU
R RH HL
R RH HR
R RH HB
R HU HR
R HR HL
R HL HB
R HB HU
! roll crank: a pin along the arm axis, 1U below it, and a coupler across in y
C R5CC D1 6,0,5.5 y x
R HLv R5CC
H R5C W8 7,0,5.5
P 6.8,0,5.5 silver
P 7.2,0,5.5 silver
H R5A W8 7,2,5.5
P 6.8,2,5.5 silver
P 7.2,2,5.5 silver
R R5C R5A
C YK5 R3 5,2,5.5 z -y
C PC5 D1 9,2,5.5 y -x
R YK5 PC5
C AE5 D1 5,-2,5.5 x y
R YK5 AE5
H GR1 W8 5,0,5.5
R GR1 WH
E rolA YK5 GR1 rest=55
E rolB AE5 GR1 rest=55
F AE5 0,0.01,0 roll
F GR1 0,-0.01,0 rollr
! AXIS 6 gripper: one jaw pivoting on an axle through the top of the hand, closing past a fixed anvil
C JAC D1 8,2,7.5 x -y
R HU JAC
H JH W8 8,1,7.5
P 8,0.8,7.5 silver
P 8,1.2,7.5 silver
C JT B7 10,1,7.5 y -x
C JTv B7 10,1,7.5 z -y
C JD R3 10,1,5.5 y -x+z
R JH JT
R JT JD
R JH JD
C JF W8 10,0,5.5
R HLv JF
! gripper crank pin on the jaw, coupler up to the slider
C G6CC D1 10,-1,7.5 x y
R JTv G6CC
H G6C W8 10,0,7.5
P 10,-0.2,7.5 silver
P 10,0.2,7.5 silver
H G6A W8 11,0,8.5
P 11,-0.2,8.5 silver
P 11,0.2,8.5 silver
R G6C G6A
C YK6 R3 11,-1,8.5 x -z
C PC6 D1 11,1,8.5 x -y
R YK6 PC6
C AE6 D1 11,-1,4.5 x z
R YK6 AE6
H GG1 W8 11,-1,6.5
C GB0 W8 9,-1,6.5
R GG1 GB0
R GB0 HBv
E griA YK6 GG1 rest=55
E griB AE6 GG1 rest=55
F AE6 0,0,0.01 grip
F GG1 0,0,-0.01 gripr
